# EAS Build upload rules for CLOSIQ (deployment prep, 2026-09-11).
#
# Verified against the installed eas-cli 21.7.0 source (build/vcs/clients/git.js,
# build/vcs/local.js): EAS clones the WHOLE git repository from its top level,
# reads .easignore from the REPOSITORY ROOT (this file — not mobile/), and when
# this file exists NO .gitignore file is applied at all. Every rule from BOTH
# /.gitignore and /mobile/.gitignore is therefore repeated below, with the
# mobile-relative anchored rules re-anchored under mobile/.
#
# Why this file exists: without it, every build uploads ~448 MB, 444 MB of
# which is `public/test samples/` — original source photos the mobile app
# never reads (the served catalog is the 58 WebP files in public/wardrobe/,
# which the mobile build doesn't bundle either; images come from the backend).
#
# SECURITY: the .env rules below keep GEMINI_API_KEY (root .env) and the local
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* dev values (mobile/.env.local) out of the EAS archive. Build-time
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* values must come from EAS environment variables instead.
# Verify with:  node scripts/check-easignore.mjs

# ---- secrets / local env (from both .gitignore files) ----
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!mobile/.env.example
*.local
*.pem
*.p8
*.p12
*.jks
*.key
*.mobileprovision

# ---- unused by the mobile build, large ----
public/test samples/
# eas-cli >= 24 uploads a shallow git clone and only deletes ignored *files*;
# its .git pack still holds every tracked blob (incl. the 444 MB of test
# photos), which made the archive 352 MB. Builds don't need git history.
.git

# ---- from /.gitignore ----
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*
node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?
mobile/.test-build

# ---- from /mobile/.gitignore (re-anchored) ----
mobile/.expo/
mobile/web-build/
mobile/expo-env.d.ts
.kotlin/
*.orig.*
.metro-health-check*
*.tsbuildinfo
mobile/ios
mobile/android
